# The one version of each toolchain, for the Mac, the Docker images and CI
# alike (the owner, 2026-11-09: "make it all consistent"). asdf's format,
# because CI's setup-python, setup-java and setup-node read it as their
# *-version-file, and mise or asdf on a Mac read it as it is. The rest
# reads it through scripts/build/toolchain.sh (`get <name>`), and what
# cannot read a file at all (a Dockerfile's FROM, the pom, the Gradle
# files, rust-toolchain.toml, .nvmrc) is written from it by
# `scripts/build/toolchain.sh`; `--check`, in CI's architecture job, fails
# on any place that differs. Bump a version here, run the script, commit
# what it changed.
